<title>GERMANY: Karstadt sees static 1996 earnings.</title>
<headline>Karstadt sees static 1996 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German retail group Karstadt AG said on Tuesday it saw little scope for an increase in its full-year 1996 profit due to slack consumer demand.  </p>
<p>The company said in an interim statement: &quot;In spite of the cost reduction measures we are pursuing we see little room to improve the group's result during the rest of the year.&quot;</p>
<p>It said it saw no improvement in consumer demand in the remaining months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
